# ALUMNUS OF THE WEEK!!! Aston Wylie is a music artist who was born in East London, South Africa and is currently based in Dubai, United Arab Emirates. Aston began his music career in Port Elizabeth whilst studying towards a bachelor's degree in music (Technology) Nelson Mandela Metropolitan University. Highly involved in the choir, Aston balanced his studies with an exciting and practice intensive choir schedule. He also participated in local shows with well known companies; Centrestage and Two-Tone Music. After graduating, Aston relocated to Cape Town where he began performing full time. It was during this period that he performed regularly as a solo artist and as a touring session musician for Majozi. He also appeared on Mnet's "The Voice SA" (season 2) and acquired the first ever double steal in the battle rounds. In 2020 Aston released his first full length album, which held 2 heavy rotation singles "Stormy Waters" and "Lose it all". Aston relocated to Dubai in 2022 and hit the ground running by performing his first show as part of an Abba tribute show at the world renowned Coca Cola Arena in Dubai. Since then, he has also performed at the Abu Dhabi F1 2022/23, FINA world diving championships 2022, and the Emirates Dubai 7s 2022/2023. He has recently released his brand new single "Butterflies" which has garnered attention from a new UAE audience as well as his South African base. #astonwylie #nelsonmandelauniversity #musicandperformingarts #TheVoice #artist #performer #eastlondon... - Nelson Mandela University - Department of Music and Performing Arts
